extraction_notes: "WB19 Australia printed 125-126 (cache p126-p127, cache page = printed folio + 1), read off the text layer in column order. Heading Navy Sailor O.C.C. and the lore on printed 125, where the stat block, headed City Navy Sailor O.C.C., runs through the MOS packages and the O.C.C. Related list; the Secondary Skills paragraph starts at the foot of printed 125 and continues on printed 126 with Standard Equipment, Vehicle, Money and Cybernetics, above the Mutants heading. || CITY RULES: the City O.C.C. list on printed 105 places the class under Other, as Naval Sailor O.C.C., below the Optional City Military O.C.C.s and prints that every Tech-City character speaks English at a minimum of 84+1D6% and is literate (+20%); the class block prints its own higher figures, which are the ones stored. The same page says a City character played outside the walls is an agent, exile, criminal, rebel or truant, or part of an all-City group; that is in GM Notes. Imported as PLAYABLE on the survey decision of 2026-10-01. || NAME AND ID: the survey reserves navy-sailor-australia because production holds a Sailor and a Navy Seaman; the display name carries (Australia). The book prints Navy Sailor O.C.C., City Navy Sailor O.C.C. and, in the lists, Naval Sailor. || GROUP: the entry sits under the Military O.C.C.s heading of printed 121 and the Navy is one of the four military departments (printed 96), so it is a Men at Arms class: occ_group men-of-arms. No Base S.D.C. is printed, only +3D6 to S.D.C., so men_of_arms is true and the 3D6 is a pool bonus. || XP: the Aero-Jock, City Trader & Naval Sailor ladder on the Experience Tables, printed 224, read off a render (level 1 prints 0,000-2000). || BONUSES: +3D6 S.D.C., +1 P.S., +1 on initiative. || MOS: the seven Military Occupational Specialty packages (pick one) are stored as seven variants, because a package grants skills and a chosen ability cannot carry skills. A package skill the O.C.C. list also grants takes the higher bonus, as the book''s note says: Gunner Weapon Systems +15 over +5, Officer Navigation +15 over +10, and Aviator Pilot Robots & Power Armor +5 over none are skill overrides. || NOT STORED, a variant cannot carry it: the related categories an MOS opens (Communications for Officers and Communications Technicians, any Electrical for Technicians, Mechanical for Mechanics, any Medical at +10% for Medics, aircraft at +10% for Aviators). The categories stored are the plain sailor''s, so the picker fails closed; the rule is in the Military Occupational Specialty ability and the related note. Communications, Espionage, Mechanical, Military, Rogue and Cowboy: None are honoured by leaving the categories out. || SKILLS: Speak English 86+3D4% is Language: Australian English at 86 with no per-level step; the 3D4 is rolled by the player and is not stored. Literacy (+20%) is Literacy: Native Language. Pilot Ship is Boat: Ships. Pilot Watercraft of choice is a pick of one from the seven other watercraft rows. Pilot Power Armor (one of choice) is Robots & Power Armor at its catalog base, a reading: no bonus is printed, and the one type is the player''s to name. Radar/Sonar Operation is Radar/Sonar Operations; Submersible Vehicle Repair is Submersible Vehicle Mechanics; Basic Cybernetics is Cybernetics: Basic; Field Expedient Surgery is Field Surgery, a reading; Demolitions: Disposal is Demolitions Disposal; Pilot Warship/Patrol Boat is Military: Warships & Patrol Boats; Pilot Helicopter and Pilot Jet Fighter are Helicopter and Military: Jet Fighters. Pilot: Any non-aircraft is the Pilot category less thirteen aircraft, spacecraft and flight-combat rows. Science: Math and Astronomy only is both Mathematics rows and Astronomy. Hand to Hand: Basic prints no upgrade price, so no hand_to_hand block is stored. Secondary skills: two at levels 1, 4, 8 and 12. No horsemanship: City troops are not trained to ride (printed 157). || MONEY: all start with one month''s pay. Enlisted sailors earn $1800 a month, technicians $2000, and gunners, medical personnel, aviators and officers $2400, +$100 per level. starting_money is 1800 on the class and the month''s pay of the MOS on each variant; reading the three technical packages (Communications Technician, Sensors Operator, Mechanic) as the technicians is a reading, the Sensors Operator being the one the book does not call a technician. || EQUIPMENT not stored as rows: the inflatable life vest, heavy-duty rainsuit, winter jacket, woolen cap, several pairs of gloves and grooming utensils have no Rifts catalog row; the power armor trooper''s medium M.D.C. body armor and power armor suit, the officer''s and the mechanic''s and medic''s extra issue, and the weapons issued for dangerous duty (an S.D.C. pistol and an energy rifle with three extra E-Clips) are conditional. All are in GM Notes. The text layer prints then- power armor suit for their. Vessels, VTOL aircraft and power armor are vehicles, named in GM Notes."
---

## Lore

The navies of Perth and Melbourne want professionalism and discipline beyond
what is asked of the average Grunt. A sailor has to be bright enough for
specialized training, steady enough to spend weeks shut inside a metal hull,
and self-motivated; a warship has no room for slackers.

Duty is on patrol boats, small ships and small to medium submersibles that
guard the harbors and waters around the two Tech-Cities. They seldom go more
than 20 miles (32 km) out, so in some ways the service is a heavily armored
coast guard rather than a blue-water navy. Power armor is used aboard ship,
in the air and underwater, and with aircraft gives air support and a quick
response.

## GM Notes

Printed 96 names the Navy as one of the four military departments and as
Perth''s strongest. The City list on printed 105 says a City character met
outside the walls is an agent, an exile, a criminal, a rebel or a truant,
unless the whole group is a City team on assignment.

Spoken English is 86% plus 3D4%, rolled once; the sheet shows 86.

The MOS is chosen as the variant. It also widens the related list, which the
sheet does not do: Officers and Communications Technicians may take any
Communications skill; Technicians any Electrical skill; Mechanics any
Mechanical skill; Medics any Medical skill at +10%; Aviators any Pilot skill,
aircraft included, at +10%.

Kit beyond what the sheet lists (printed 126): an inflatable life vest that
supports light to medium body armor, a heavy-duty rainsuit, a winter jacket,
a woolen cap, several pairs of gloves and grooming utensils. Power armor
troops have medium M.D.C. body armor and their power armor suit. Officers
also have a pocket computer, a Pocket Digital Disc player, tactical and
history manuals on disc, a full-sized computer in their quarters, and
sidearms: an energy pistol and a Vibro-Knife or Neural Mace. Mechanics are
issued basic tool kits and have the run of the ship''s mechanics bays; medics
have personal first-aid kits and access to the ship''s hospital areas.

Weapons are kept in lockers aboard ship, because sailors seldom fight
directly and to prevent mutiny. On dangerous duty, such as a small patrol
ship, a sailor is issued an S.D.C. pistol and an energy rifle with three
extra E-Clips; on bigger ships rifles and sidearms are issued only under
combat conditions.

Vehicle: none of his own. The sailor serves aboard a naval vessel, from
patrol boat to submarine or warship; aviators and some others are assigned a
VTOL aircraft and/or power armor for operations, not for personal use.

Pay: enlisted sailors $1800 a month, technicians $2000, and gunners, medical
personnel, aviators and officers $2400, +$100 per level of experience.
Quarters aboard ship and a berth ashore, food, clothing and medical treatment
are provided.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'navy-sailor-australia');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'navy-sailor-australia';

